or each judge was based on Total Points awarded by that judge to the pairs, with the tiebreaker being Sporting Merit (2nd mark).  Final placement was determined by a Majority Placement rule.  Thus, if a pair were ranked first by a majority of the judges, that pair was placed first overall, and the process was repeated for each place.  If no absolute majority for a place existed, the tiebreakers were, in order: 1) Total Ordinals, 2) Total Points, 3) Compulsory Figure Points."]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Judge #1"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5001985"} "Ernst Herz"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUT"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUT.png"}] "AUT"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Judge #2"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/99117"} "Henry Yglesias"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Judge #3"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5002636"} "J. Künzli"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SUI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SUI.png"}] "SUI"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Judge #4"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5002115"} "Francis Pigueron"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Judge #5"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5002913"} "Josef Fellner"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUT"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central